    785  f0f9							; (2026-10-15) GRP0 blank REMOVED: +5c pushed the rows0/1 setup
    786  f0f9							; segment to 75c armed (>=74 = write lands next line = +1 stall line
    787  f0f9							; = whole-screen shift). The blank only traded a stale-byte duplicate
    788  f0f9							; for a blank line at band boundaries — shipped pre-99b8e86 without
    789  f0f9							; either; case15 filters zero writes so the Y-align guard is unaffected.
    790  f0f9							; --- Scanlines this pass: rows 0/1 = 48; row 2 = 36+off (tide, CollisionX).
    791  f0f9							; The bottom water strip (last 12-off lines, bottom_band_plan rule 2)
    792  f0f9							; renders in .WaterRow after this pass — its own setup line + (11-off)
    793  f0f9							; bodies keeps the row-2 total at 49 lines (setup+48) exactly.
    794  f0f9							; Split tail (2026-10-05, row1 setup gap 77->74): row1 gate used to pay
    795  f0f9							; `bne` 3c to skip the tide load AND share the WSYNC — gap was 77 (stall,
    796  f0f9							; +1 line/frame). Rows 0/1 now store+WSYNC before the tide block, then
    797  f0f9							; jmp over it (+3c charged to the FIRST body line = 66max+3jmp+3WSYNC
    798  f0f9							; = 72 <=76). Row2 path byte-identical in cost (cpx/beqT/lda/sta/WSYNC
    799  f0f9							; = 11+3 = 76, zero margin — the `beq` target is 9 bytes ahead, same
    800  f0f9							; page, T=3c; do not let this block grow toward a page edge).
    801  f0f9							; A1 gap fix (2026-10-05): `sta Temp` (+3c in .Row) pushed gaps to
    802  f0f9							; 77/79 = stall EVERY frame (265-line frames). `sta LineCount` moved
    803  f0f9							; AFTER `sta WSYNC` — same bytes, -3c from the gap window, +3c to the
    804  f0f9							; first body line (66max+3LC[+3jmp]+3WSYNC = 75 rows0/1, 72 row2).
    805  f0f9							; LineCount is not read until the line's `dec` tail — the early store
    806  f0f9							; was never required; keep the store strictly between WSYNC and .Line.
    807  f0f9		       e0 02		      cpx	#TILE_ROWS-1
    808  f0fb		       f0 09		      beq	.RowLinesTide	; row 2: tide count (36+off) from CollisionX
    809  f0fd							; rows 0/1: fixed 48 lines (the vcrunch shutter slice derive is gone).
    810  f0fd		       a9 30		      lda	#48
    811  f0ff							; --- Sync to next scanline (rows 0/1) ---
    812  f0ff		       85 02		      sta	WSYNC
    813  f101		       85 84		      sta	LineCount
    814  f103		       4c 0c f1 	      jmp	.Line
    815  f106				   .RowLinesTide
    816  f106		       a5 8b		      lda	CollisionX	; 36..39 — VBL tide calc (see VBL comment)
    817  f108							; --- Sync to next scanline (row 2; falls straight into .Line) ---
    818  f108		       85 02		      sta	WSYNC
    819  f10a		       85 84		      sta	LineCount
    820  f10c
    821  f10c				   .Line
    822  f10c							; --- Player sprite: color for THIS line, graphics byte for NEXT line ---
    823  f10c							; GRP0 written on line S displays on line S+1 (latched at the sprite's
    824  f10c							; window start after the write) — index graphics with A0+1 ($ff wraps
    825  f10c							; to 0 = row0 on the line before the sprite).
    826  f10c							; Running-Y: Y = A0 = Scanline - RoomY is computed ONCE at kernel entry
    827  f10c							; (sec/sbc RoomY/tay); .Line's iny advances it (Y = A0+1 after the
    828  f10c							; graphics write = A0 of the next line). Nothing between rows may touch
    829  f10c							; Y — the water-strip band-color read is an inlined `lda` (Y untouched).
    830  f10c							; Cycle budget — MEASURED (sim_frame_budget, bugs.md #29 Class A):
    831  f10c							; the old worst path (in-window color/beam/GRP0 + object in-range) was
    832  f10c							; 78c: WSYNC write landed 2c into the next line -> full-line stall ->
    833  f10c							; +1 scanline on every frame whose object window overlapped the A0=11
    834  f10c							; line (24 stalls in the SIM_LEVEL=2 window, always even frames —
    835  f10c							; SelectActiveObject parity rotation). Root fix: the color/beam gate
    836  f10c							; below stops at A0=10; row 11 inherits row 10's COLUP0/ENAM0 writes
    837  f10c							; (PlayerColTable/BeamMask [10]==[11], verify_build asserts) because
    838  f10c							; GRP0 row11 is fetched on line A0=10 already ("row11 shows via
    839  f10c							; line10"). Worst path measured 2026-10-15 (vcrunch jitter hunt):
    840  f10c							; in-window color/beam/GRP0 + object in-range = 69c between WSs,
    841  f10c							; start-to-start d=72 — was 73/76 (= stall zone 74-76, whole-screen
    842  f10c							; +1-line jitter) until the dead `cpy #12 / bcs .GrpZero` (4c, never
    843  f10c							; taken on the A0<=10 color path) moved to .GrpSkip. Budget: work
    844  f10c							; <= 70c / d <= 73 — a 74-76 segment stalls a full scanline.
    845  f10c							; ObjSprites+71 must stay in the $FExx page (else lda ObjSprites,X
    846  f10c							; page-crosses, +1c on the GRP1 fetch) — verify_build enforces this.
    847  f10c							; Branch targets all same-page (3c taken) and BeamMask operand in $FExx
    848  f10c							; (4c fetch, no-cross — verify_build S2.2 guard).
    849  f10c							; GRP1 object section clobbers X (ObjSprites index) — row counter lives in
    850  f10c							; RowIdx and X is reloaded after bne. Row-advance +6c on the .Row setup
    851  f10c							; scanline (segment 63c -> 69c <= 76c): frame length unchanged.
    852  f10c							; The old Scanline/sec/sbc/tay prefix cost 10c more (body 66c -> WSYNC
    853  f10c							; write on cycle 76 = one cycle late): WSYNC stalled a full line per
    854  f10c							; overlapping scanline — stretched cave row, HUD pushed down, and with
    855  f10c							; GRP1 flicker rotation the frame length alternated (one-tile oscillation).
    856  f10c							; Keep the hot path at <= 70c work: an overrun duplicates the scanline.
    857  f10c		       c0 0b		      cpy	#PLAYER_SPRITE_H - 1
    858  f10e		       b0 40		      bcs	.GrpSkip	; A0 >= 11 (incl $ff): no color/beam this line.
    859  f110							; A0=11 skips too (Class-A stall line): rows
    860  f110							; 10/11 share color+beam bytes, so row 10's
    861  f110							; writes are still in effect here.
    862  f110		       b9 f5 f8 	      lda	PlayerColTable,Y	; 4c — per-row color from ROM
    863  f113		       85 06		      sta	COLUP0	; COLUP0 has no latch: applies to this line
    864  f115							; --- Laser S2.2: ENAM0 = beam mask for THIS line (in-window only) ---
    865  f115							; BeamMask = {0,0,2,0,0...} → ENAM0 on RoomY+2 only (single yellow
    866  f115							; strip — user directive 2026-10-08: the red row-3 strip is gone;
    867  f115							; kill window in LaserHitTestBody keeps rows RoomY+2..3 = superset).
    868  f115							; In-window path is the only safe place (Y<11 guaranteed); outside the
    869  f115							; window ENAM0 keeps its last in-window write ($00 at A0=10) — no HUD
    870  f115							; artifact. Table lives in $FExx (no-cross = 4c, verify_build guard).
    871  f115		       b9 db fe 	      lda	BeamMask,Y	; 4c (no-cross $FExx) — table MUST stay $FExx
    872  f118		       25 c0		      and	LaserState	; 3c — beam gate: b1 armed only while fire held
    873  f11a		       85 1d		      sta	ENAM0	; 3c (bar showed without fire before this)
    874  f11c		       c8		      iny		; Y = A0+1 ($ff wraps to 0 = sprite row 0).
    875  f11d							;   Color/beam gate entered only with A0<=10
    876  f11d							;   -> after iny Y<=11: always fetchable, so
    877  f11d							;   the old `cpy #PLAYER_SPRITE_H / bcs
    878  f11d							;   .GrpZero` here was DEAD 4c on the worst
    879  f11d							;   path (2+2, never taken — A0=11+ never
    880  f11d							;   reaches it, it goes to bcs .GrpSkip).
    881  f11d		       b1 86		      lda	(Grp0Ptr),Y	; 5c — byte for the NEXT scanline
    882  f11f		       85 1b		      sta	GRP0
    883  f121				   .Grp1
