   3445  fdd0							; BombEnemyBlast — bank2 entry tramp ($FDD8, lamp-safe S9 2026-10-07): the
   3446  fdd0							; BombTick `jsr` lands here (bank0), `sta $1FF8` switches to bank2, the `jmp`
   3447  fdd0							; is fetched from bank2's byte-identical mirror at this same address and
   3448  fdd0							; lands on the body at $FD87 (the lamp type-check reads enemy records that
   3449  fdd0							; live in bank2). Body tail-jmps ReturnPad ($FBF8); A = 1 kill (BombTick
   3450  fdd0							; awards +50 — pads cannot nest), 0 none. Old inline body ($F87F, 66B)
   3451  fdd0							; deleted: the region re-packs into the gap before the $FBD6 fold pin
   3452  fdd0							; (pre-pad headroom stays 1B — pins absorb upstream shrink, not the org).
   3453  fdd0							; TWIN: bank2.asm mirrors these exact 6 bytes at $FDD8 (the pad after
   3454  fdd0							; .HOVdone). The PickPlayerFrame pin that used to absorb the size is gone
   3455  fdd0							; (retired 2026-10-20); the $FC49 / $FBF8 pins bound this block today.
   3456  fdd0							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   3457  fdd0		       00 00 00 00*	      .ds	$FDD8 - *, 0	; pin: bank2's blast-tramp mirror is at $FDD8
   3458  fdd8				   BombEnemyBlast
